<keymap>
  <!-- Copied from what actually works on a Byintek U4 projector, read off its
       POV IL profile on 9 October 2026, and written to be right on the other
       two boxes in the house as well.

       One file, every input kind, because the same press arrives differently
       on each: the projector's remote as a *joystick* (it reports to Android
       as one), the Mi Box's as a *remote*, a PC keyboard as *backspace*, and
       Android's own back gesture as *appcommand*. A keymap naming only one of
       them fixes one box and leaves the others as they were.

       Two separate problems, one file.

       One: that remote reports as an Android joystick rather than a remote,
       so Kodi sees button numbers and binds nothing to them. Its Back key is
       button 6 and its Menu key button 7, which the peripheral buttonmap
       already calls "back" and "start"; these lines give those features
       something to do.

       Two: Back during fullscreen video minimises playback and leaves it
       running, which on a projector reads as "the film would not close".
       Scoped to FullscreenVideo alone, so Back still means Back in menus. -->
  <global>
    <joystick>
      <back>Back</back>
      <start>ContextMenu</start>
    </joystick>
  </global>
  <FullscreenVideo>
    <keyboard>
      <backspace>Stop</backspace>
    </keyboard>
    <remote>
      <back>Stop</back>
    </remote>
    <gamepad>
      <back>Stop</back>
    </gamepad>
    <appcommand>
      <browser_back>Stop</browser_back>
    </appcommand>
  </FullscreenVideo>
</keymap>
